<title>TURKEY: Turkey leaves grain, vegoil import taxes same in 97.</title>
<headline>Turkey leaves grain, vegoil import taxes same in 97.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey has not changed customs taxes on imports of wheat, barley, corn, durum, sorghum, rice and sunflower seed oil in its newly-published 1997 import regime, the Official Gazette said.</p>
<p>It said taxes for imports of milling wheat, durum, barley and corn remained at 15 percent, those on two types of sunflower oil were unchanged at 39 percent and 50 percent respectively.</p>
<p>The government had raised taxes on the grains to 15 percent from three percent in September.</p>
<p>Rice and paddy import taxes also remained the same at 35 and 27 percent respectively. Sorghum imports have a three percent tax.</p>
<p>The 1997 import regime, published in the Official Gazette, has been held since January by the government due to a dispute between the two coalition partners over importtaxes on some items. --Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
